  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nSee https://hud.pytorch.org/hud/pytorch/pytorch/e3ebf364e6d2fb8008da113a596d3cc426ba9c79/1?per_page=50&name_filter=inductor-periodic&mergeEphemeralLF=true\n\nI've scrolled down to page 7 (Aug 11th , i.e. a week ago) and noticed that may be https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/160255 introduced more regressions, see\nhttps://hud.pytorch.org/hud/pytorch/pytorch/e3ebf364e6d2fb8008da113a596d3cc426ba9c79/7?per_page=50&name_filter=inductor-periodic&mergeEphemeralLF=true\n\n<img width=\"990\" height=\"189\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93c1335d-f407-45e4-b1aa-ed4ae23499f8\" />\n\n\nI've scrolled down to [page 50](https://hud.pytorch.org/hud/pytorch/pytorch/e3ebf364e6d2fb8008da113a596d3cc426ba9c79/36?per_page=50&name_filter=inductor-periodic&mergeEphemeralLF=true)\n\nAnd still see the same failure patterns persisting for 1+ month:\n- test (dynamic_inductor_torchbench) fails `functorch_dp_cifar10`\n- sm86-periodic-dynamo-benchmarks / test (aot_eager_timm fails `mobilenetv3_large_100`\n-  linux-jammy-cpu-py3.9-gcc11-inductor / test (cpu_inductor_amp_freezing_torchbench fails `detectron2_fcos_r_50_fpn`\nAnd so on...\n### Versions\n\nCI\n\ncc @ezyang @gchanan @zou3519 @kadeng @msaroufim @seemethere @pytorch/pytorch-dev-infra @chauhang @penguinwu",
